ed history. Each employee generates $105K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Ryan Specialty Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.9B market cap on $3.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 7% cost of capital, a 10-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $641M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 10.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 60/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 20% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Insider Selling: Ryan Specialty (NYSE:RYAN) CEO Sells 50,000 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/insider-selling-ryan-specialty-nyseryan-ceo-sells-50000-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794528543.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Ryan Specialty Holdings Inc's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ryan-specialty-holdings-incs-dividend-101030235.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794305430.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},